It is structurally aligned, but I would not freeze it until these are corrected:

Workflow IDs may be fake/new

CES requires workflows to come from workflows.generated.ts, not invented IDs. The docs say sprint work must use compiled workflow definitions and the sprint cannot edit workflow definitions directly. 


So IDs like CL-WF-POC-AUDIT-001 are only valid if they actually exist or are added to workflow source and compiled.

Templates cannot bypass the calendar source

The authoritative load point is MANDATED_EVENTS_EXPANDED; sprint loading must be deterministic from calendar sources. 


Final version should output actual RegulatoryEvent objects, not only templates, unless the generator writes into that source.

Each generated event must decompose into execution units

CES requires Event → Workflow → Execution Unit, not just event → workflow. 


Each workflow must still produce the five phases: Preparation, Documentation, Review, Signature, Audit. 


Recurring controls must stay separate

Do not mix the 32 audit workflows with CES recurring units R1–R8. Those are auto-generated per sprint. 


Completion rules must be enforced

No item is complete until evidence, signatures, and audit index entry exist. 


Final correction
The final model should be:

Existing/compiled workflows
→ audit event templates
→ generated RegulatoryEvent objects
→ MANDATED_EVENTS_EXPANDED
→ sprint loader
→ execution units
→ board states
→ evidence/signature/audit closure
So: yes, the concept is final. The dataset is not final until workflow IDs are verified against the actual generated workflow list.



